<title>USA: Franklin Electronic sets buyback plan.</title>
<headline>Franklin Electronic sets buyback plan.</headline>
<dateline>BURLINGTON, N.J. 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Franklin Electronic Publishers Inc on Monday said it plans to repurchase up to $5.0 million of its common stock over time in the open market.</p>
<p>The company's stock is currently trading at about $11 per share.  The company, in its most recent earnings release, said it had 8.1 million shares outstanding as of June 30.</p>
<p>Franklin makes handheld electronic consumer devices, phone components and electronic equipment.</p>
</text>
